author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: "The canonical related kind carries a declared bound in the same registry as every other dependency kind, so the largest edge population is no longer the only unbounded one; The declared quantity is a composition ratio rather than a raw count, so semantic edge share is enforceable independently of how many edges the graph holds in total; The alias spelling and the canonical spelling resolve to one declaration, so a bound can never be satisfied by writing the spelling that is not bounded; A negative control proves the bound fails when an associative-only enrichment dilutes semantic share and passes when the same count of typed edges is added instead; Semantic share is reported by the graph audit profile, so dilution is visible from the governance surface without reading the ratchet declaration file"
